<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puerto Rico</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puerto Rico is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, colonised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from the early sixteenth century. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, it was among the last remnants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> after the American independence wars of the early nineteenth century. Spain lost it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puerto-rico.jpg" alt="Puerto Rico" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: Cerejota · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Puerto_Rico.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
